  "instance_name": "racial_inequality",
  "label": "The systemic and structural disadvantages faced by certain racial groups",
  "description": "Racial inequality refers to the systemic and structural disadvantages faced by certain racial groups, often resulting in higher rates of violence, poverty, and discrimination. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to downplay or justify racially motivated violence, thereby challenging the concept of racial inequality. This requires understanding of the concept of racial inequality and its implications.",
